WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:07.840
Japan is facing a serious conundrum. It&nbsp;
has sunk so much money into the Olympics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:15.680
Officially, $15.4 billion US dollars. And if&nbsp;
Tokyo cancels the Games, the country stands to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.880
lose an estimated $16.5 billion. So organizers&nbsp;
are loathe to stop the Games. But citizens see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:29.680
a public health danger if the event moves forward.&nbsp;
The majority do not want it to happen - especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:38.080
because most of the country remains un-vaccinated.
Aussie Spirit - the Australian Olympic softball&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:42.080
team - is the first international&nbsp;
squad to arrive in Japan.&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.880
And they're facing unprecedented&nbsp;
restrictions - no restaurants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:54.160
no sightseeing, and certainly no socializing.
"I think these athletes well know that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.320
have to take great responsibility for their own&nbsp;
behavior as well. They’re committed to do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.400
they’re committed to not only look after&nbsp;
themselves but do the right thing by the Japanese&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.680
population as well and be ready for the Games.
Most people in Japan don't want the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.760
Olympics Games to happen.
They're questioning the sense of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:18.160
15,000 Olympic and Paralympic athletes from&nbsp;
more than 200 countries traveling to Japan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.200
at a time when serious COVID-19&nbsp;
cases have recently hit new highs.&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.240
And the nation's slow vaccination&nbsp;
roll out isn't helping either.&nbsp;

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.040
"Japan has been working hard to roll vaccines out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.560
but demand did not match with&nbsp;
supply in the first place."&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.560
Japanese Olympic athletes&nbsp;
are now being offered jabs.&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:53.840
But only about two and a half percent of Japan's&nbsp;
population has been fully vaccinated so far.&nbsp;

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.920
Despite all this, the&nbsp;
organizers are standing firm.&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.960
"Sports events are held all over the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.560
and as I've said, there are no examples of&nbsp;
COVID-19 clusters of the infection spreading.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.920
Therefore, we believe that we don't&nbsp;
need to think about canceling now."&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:24.560
The arrival of Australia's softball team is a&nbsp;
huge show of confidence in the beleaguered event.&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:32.320
All team members tested negative after landing.
But the question remains - will this be enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:36.640
to restore the confidence of the&nbsp;
Japanese public in the Games?

